sketchBlocks.bodyMarkdown:
Custom properties give repeated design values meaningful names so one decision can be reused throughout the stylesheet.

**Worked example:**

```css
:root {
  --color-accent: #1d4ed8;
  --space-section: 1.5rem;
}
```

**Line by line:** `:root {` creates a high-level place for shared values. `--color-accent` stores a color decision. `--space-section` stores a spacing decision. The closing brace ends the shared-value rule.

